{number: 87}
{title: What a Friend We Have in Jesus}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] What a friend we have in Jesus,
[F] All our sins and griefs to [C] bear!
What a privilege to [G7] carry
[C] Everything to God in prayer!
[G7] Oh, what peace we often forfeit,
[C] Oh, what [F] needless pain we [C] bear,
All because we do not [F] carry
[C] Everything to [G7] God in [C] prayer!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Have we trials and temptations?
[F] Is there trouble any-[C] where?
We should never be dis-[G7] couraged,
[C] Take it to the Lord in prayer.
[G7] Can we find a friend so faithful,
[C] Who will [F] all our sorrows [C] share?
Jesus knows our every [F] weakness;
[C] Take it to the [G7] Lord in [C] prayer.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Are we weak and heavy-laden,
[F] Cumbered with a load of [C] care?
Precious Savior, still our [G7] refuge
[C] Take it to the Lord in prayer.
[G7] Do thy friends despise, forsake thee?
[C] Take it [F] to the Lord in [C] prayer;
In His arms He’ll take and [F] shield thee,
[C] Thou wilt find a [G7] solace [C] there.
{end_of_verse}
